@baseUrl = http://localhost:5128
@HostAddress = {{baseUrl}}
@companyAdminEmail = admin@al-salamah.com
@companyAdminPassword = User@123456
@missingId = 7c1e4d55-9a02-4b31-8f6e-2d47b9a0c318

### =====================================================================
### 14. FIELD OPERATIONS WBS & EXIF VERIFICATION (FR-OPS-01..06, FR-AUD-01..04)
### =====================================================================
### Site execution: the Operations Officer builds a Work Breakdown Structure of tracks, milestones
### and granular tasks; technicians work their own tasks and upload geotagged proof; the server
### reads GPS and capture time out of the image bytes, measures the distance from the facility pin
### with the Haversine formula, and records a verdict.
###
### Three outcomes, one refusal. A photo inside the 300 m geofence and freshly captured verifies.
### One with a location that is not the site is kept and flagged — the flag is the audit record.
### One with no metadata routes to a supervisor's written justification (FR-AUD-04), because iOS
### and Android strip EXIF under ordinary privacy settings. Only a photo captured outside the
### 6-hour freshness window is refused outright (FR-AUD-03), since it is not evidence about today.
###
### The full lifecycle — the preset, the micro-FSM, all three photo outcomes against real JPEG EXIF
### bytes, the obstacle escalation machine, and closing out to PreClosure — is covered by
### FieldOperationsLifecycleTests, GeodesyTests, PhotoVerificationPolicyTests (xUnit) and a 63-check
### scripted live run against SQL Server. This suite is a smoke test of the surface with explicit
### assertions. Field casing is camelCase (D-8).

### 14.1 Company Admin login
# @name companyAdminLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{companyAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{companyAdminPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@companyAdminToken = {{companyAdminLogin.data.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Planning the Work Breakdown Structure (FR-OPS-01/02/03)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14.2 The plan for a job that does not exist -> 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 14.3 Applying the three-silo preset to a job that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/sections/apply-standard
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 14.4 A track code that is not upper snake_case -> 400
### Codes identify a track within its project so reports can key on them, which only works if they
### are stable and machine-safe.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/sections
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "sectionCode": "not a code!", "sectionNameAr": "مسار" }

?? status == 400

### 14.5 A track with no Arabic name -> 400
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/sections
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "sectionCode": "FIRE_ALARM", "sectionNameAr": "" }

?? status == 400

### 14.6 A milestone whose deadline precedes its start date -> 400
### A milestone that reads as overdue the moment it is created poisons every report downstream.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/sprints
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "sectionId": "{{missingId}}",
  "sprintTitle": "Phase 1: Ground floor loop",
  "targetStartDate": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "targetCompletionDate": "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z"
}

?? status == 400

### 14.7 A milestone under a track that does not exist -> 404
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/sprints
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "sectionId": "{{missingId}}", "sprintTitle": "Phase 1: Ground floor loop" }

?? status == 404

### 14.8 A task with no title -> 400
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "sprintId": "{{missingId}}", "taskTitle": "" }

?? status == 400

### 14.9 A task under a milestone that does not exist -> 404
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "sprintId": "{{missingId}}", "taskTitle": "Mount main control panel" }

?? status == 404

### 14.10 Removing a task that does not exist -> 404
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Working a task — the two sides of FR-OPS-05
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14.11 CompanyAdmin holds no FieldOps.Execute, so the mobile list refuses them -> 403
### Doing the work and inspecting it are separate grants. Management plans and supervises; nobody
### holds both sides of the verification gate, or it would be ceremonial.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 403

### 14.12 Likewise for starting a task -> 403
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 403

### 14.13 And for submitting one -> 403
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 403

### 14.14 Reviewing work is the supervisor's side, which management does hold -> 404 on the task
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "approve": true }

?? status == 404

### 14.15 Returning work without saying what is wrong -> 400
### The worker acts on this alone, from site, so "redo" is not an instruction.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "approve": false, "reworkReason": "no" }

?? status == 400

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Photo verification (FR-AUD)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14.16 Reading a task's proof when the task does not exist -> 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 14.17 Justifying a photo with a one-word reason -> 400
### The justification is the entire substitute for an automated check, so a token override is worse
### than none: it creates a paper trail that looks like diligence.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-photos/{{missingId}}/justify
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "justification": "ok" }

?? status == 400

### 14.18 Justifying a photo that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-photos/{{missingId}}/justify
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "justification": "Attended site with the technician; the device strips GPS by policy." }

?? status == 404

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Site obstacles (FR-OPS-06)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14.19 The obstacle list for a job that does not exist -> 200 with an empty list
### A sub-collection filter, not a lookup: no blockers on an unknown job is the honest answer, and
### the job's own endpoints already 404 for it.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/execution-plan/obstacles
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 200

### 14.20 Reporting a blocker is the worker's side -> 403 for management
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/field-tasks/{{missingId}}/obstacles
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "description": "Civil works have not poured the slab in the riser cupboard yet." }

?? status == 403

### 14.21 An unrecognised obstacle action -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/site-obstacles/{{missingId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "action": "ignore" }

?? status == 400

### 14.22 Resolving a blocker without recording how -> 400
### A stoppage is part of the project's account of itself; "resolved" with no notes records nothing.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/site-obstacles/{{missingId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "action": "resolve" }

?? status == 400

### 14.23 Transitioning a blocker that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/site-obstacles/{{missingId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "action": "triage" }

?? status == 404

